  "difficulty_reason": "After the ordinary Atkinson-Wilcox expansion and fixed-energy inverse-scattering uniqueness are supplied, the author must still recover every complex asymptotic coefficient from imaginary values by a two-point residual induction. That source-local argument is then combined with analytic continuation in both Green-function variables and a two-step passage from planar data to the full scattering amplitude, retaining complex-valued potentials under the explicit solvability condition. This complete inverse-recovery chain, rather than a routine continuation exercise, is substantially beyond ordinary PhD qualification problems.",
